> Aside from the previous poster, you should concentrate on getting your
> bashing/projectile skills up. I generally try to get at least skilled in
> one weapon before entering the mines. Armor helps for *all* types of
> characters. If you can't get hit easily, you don't take damage and you
> use less food. Don't encumber youself beyond burdened and drop anything
> that it making you burdened when you fight (if you are burdened in the
> upper levels and *really* want to exercise...). Try to set up chests in
> the branches of the dungeon to keep you stash. I keep one at the top of
> the mines by the stairs and one at the bottom of sokoban and sometimes
> one halfway between the two. Use your pet to check which armor you can
> use and wear the stuff you *know* not to be cursed so you can get your
> AC down. I do this the first time after returning from the mines, but
> have at least +0 of anything I can wear unless casting is *really*
> important at that point - say for healing or the sleep spell.

